From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: an8855: leave room for a second 802.1Q tag

The switch's global RX length (GMACCR) is sized for one tag: MTU +
ETH_HLEN + MTK_TAG_LEN + ETH_FCS_LEN, 1522 bytes at MTU 1500. The
an8855-8021q tagger sends a VLAN upper's frame with its own tag only, so
one tag is enough for a port or a VLAN upper of it, but a VLAN upper of
a VLAN upper (QinQ, wan.20.30) is [20][30] on the CPU link and on the
wire: a 1500-byte packet makes a 1526-byte frame.

The switch drops such frames at the MAC RX of the port they enter, the
CPU port included, and counts them in RxBadPktBytes. Measured on a
Xiaomi AX3000T v2 with wan.20.30: every frame above 1522 bytes was
dropped in both directions, so TCP over the QinQ interface moved no data
at all, on the host path and offloaded by the NSS firmware alike.

Add one VLAN_HLEN, which selects the 1536-byte setting at MTU 1500. Do it
in either tag mode: the NSS bring-up switches the conduit from mtk to
an8855-8021q at run time, after DSA programmed the CPU port's MTU, and
the register is only rewritten on an MTU change. (A version that added
the tag in 8021q mode only was measured to change nothing for exactly
that reason.)

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/an8855.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/an8855.c
@@ -1446,6 +1446,18 @@
 
 	/* RX length also includes Ethernet header, MTK tag, and FCS length */
 	length = new_mtu + ETH_HLEN + MTK_TAG_LEN + ETH_FCS_LEN;
+	/* ...and room for a second 802.1Q tag. The limit applies at the MAC
+	 * RX of every port, the CPU port included, and counts every tag in the
+	 * frame. With the an8855-8021q tagger the MTK tag's 4 bytes cover one
+	 * tag, but an MTU-sized frame can carry two: a VLAN upper of a VLAN
+	 * upper (QinQ: wan.20.30 is [20][30] on the CPU link and on the wire,
+	 * 1526 bytes at MTU 1500), or a customer-tagged frame in a VLAN-unaware
+	 * bridge. Not only in 8021q mode: the tagger can be switched at run
+	 * time (the NSS bring-up moves the conduit from mtk to an8855-8021q
+	 * after boot), and this register is only rewritten when the CPU port's
+	 * MTU changes, not when the tag protocol does.
+	 */
+	length += VLAN_HLEN;
 	if (length <= 1522)
 		val = AN8855_MAX_RX_PKT_1518_1522;
 	else if (length <= 1536)
